<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-HINGIS ROMPS INTO LAST 16.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HINGIS ROMPS INTO LAST 16.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's Martina Hingis moved towards the Australian Open final with a 6-2 6-1 victory over Barbara Schett on Saturday.</p>
<p>The 16-year-old, seeded number four but seen as the main rival to world number one Steffi Graf, displayed the full range of strokes as she crushed the Austrian in just 50 minutes for a place in the last 16.</p>
<p>&quot;It was almost a practice,&quot; Hingis said.</p>
<p>Hingis, bidding to become the youngest grand slam champion in the open era, will next meet Ruxandra Dragomir of Romania, who beat American Kristina Brandi in another third round match.</p>
